# Intentionally empty, and committed on purpose.
#
# `pnpm gen` passes this file to `wrangler types --env-file`, which *replaces* the default
# `.env` / `.dev.vars` loading. Without it, `wrangler types` describes the machine it ran
# on: a local `DATABASE_URL` or `MEDIA_PUBLIC_URL` is baked into the committed
# `worker-configuration.d.ts` as an `Env` field, so the file differs per developer and
# `pnpm check` fails on a fresh clone for a reason that looks like a code error.
#
# Runtime values do not belong here. They are read through `$env/dynamic/private`, which
# is deliberately untyped, and are supplied locally by `.env` / `.dev.vars` and in
# production by `wrangler secret put`. Only the bindings and `vars` declared in
# `wrangler.jsonc` should reach the generated file.
#
# Do not add variables to this file.
